I've written the subject review for the Austin Abrams draft to `docs/content-analysis/pipeline-logs/2026-09-11_06-00-04-236_austin-abrams/review-subject.json`. It passes the review schema check, the two checksums match the request, and every quoted passage matches the draft word for word. I changed no other files and published nothing.

To check it, I reopened seven of the key sources myself: Coup de Main, Hunger, both Hollywood Reporter pieces, the Sarasota Herald-Tribune, Screen Rant's Whalefall interview and Dread Central. Every quote I checked appears in the source as printed. The problems are in which parts of those quotes were kept, not invented material.

**Four major findings:**
1. **The safety quote is cut short.** On *Resident Evil*, Abrams said he was "really hoping you don't slip" and also didn't want to ruin the shot. The draft keeps only the shot, then uses that to claim his "own safety… drops out of view." It also leaves out that the Whalefall director, Brian Duffield, said Abrams "never got hurt" and meant the "you'll die" line admiringly.
2. **His own account of choosing roles is missing.** Asked in 2025 how he picks roles, he described an inner feeling of "I have to do this. I can't let this go," and said the pull came from the director and the character together. The draft drops that and turns one promotional line into "his enthusiasm is kindled by someone else's." Without it, the draft's case against Type 4 about *Weapons* no longer holds, because he did say what the part offered him.
3. **"Too little to say" and "interchangeable" are overreach.** The age-13 Facebook story was said with a laugh. In the same answer he gave the reason the draft says he didn't give: he isn't interested in showing people his life. The "*Wolfs* wasn't me" line, read in context, is gratitude and disbelief at working with his childhood idols.
4. **The closing "test" is already answered.** The ending asks whether he'll ever commit this hard to a project without an admired person at its center. But the article's own hook shows he already did with *Whalefall*, a role he won by audition, and no source says he took it for a particular person.

**Two minor findings:**
- The draft says "his parents" took time to accept acting, but only his father did.
- The description and opening use his 2019 "somewhat frightening" remark in the present tense and drop "somewhat." The description also states the director's joke about fatal stunts as fact.

I marked five passages to protect, including the separation of the reporter's "loyal gesture" wording from Abrams's own words and the refusal to invent a childhood wound. I flagged the typing as contested, so the full six-reviewer panel is required. The draft's medium confidence in Type 9 should be looked at again after findings 2 and 4 are fixed.
